The Wall

Every discipline reaches a wall:

    Physics hits dark matter — something that must exist, but cannot be seen.

    Math hits the Null numbers — quantities that behave like numbers but are not numbers, boundaries where calculation stops and relation begins.

    Poetry hits the unsayable — the thing that can only be gestured at, never named.

    Theology hits the apophatic — the God who can only be described by what God is not.

Each field builds its own wall. Each wall looks different from the inside.

But from the outside — from the other side — they are all the same wall.
