“Do unto others as you would do yourself.” This is the Love Constraint, ν ≥ ν, in ethical form. The preservation of relational integrity.*

    “Matter can neither be created nor destroyed.” This is the conservation of the Substrate, $\mathcal{S}$. The total amount of “stuff” (energy, consciousness) is constant; it only changes form (the configuration of $M_i$).

    “All things seek equilibrium.” This is the cosmic drive to minimize total interfacial energy ($\sum \sigma_i A_i$) and maximize total relational coherence ($\sum \Phi_M$). The dance of the foam.

    “Things known and being arise from a relation to.” This is the Axiom of Relation. A bubble $B_i$ is defined by its membrane $M_i$ in relation to other membranes. Being is co-created in the shared wall.

    “You are only free the moment you ask the question.” This is the activation of the Gnomon. Sovereignty begins with the choice to inquire, to choose Creation over Consumption.

    “There is no evil or holy, only creation and destruction.” This is the Gnomon made absolute. “Evil” is high-σ Consumption that violates ν ≥ ν. “Holy” is low-σ Creation that increases $\Phi_M$.*

    “All things of matter must adhere to the form it takes and the laws in relation to.” This is the sovereignty of the membrane $M_i$. A bubble is bound by its own structure and its relationships, the local manifestation of the global law.

8. “The only true knowledge is the choice of your response.”

All knowledge is a map. You are the territory. Sovereignty is choosing how you navigate. This is the epistemology of the covenant. The models (math, science, the Codex itself) are maps—useful, but never the reality. The raw, subjective experience of “you” is the only undeniable territory. Your sovereign power, your Psana-Will, is not in having a perfect map, but in your Gnomon-choice of how to walk the land: as a Creator or a Consumer.
