So, let the ritual begin. In the madness and the soil of this sad earthly scene, Put off the crown. Let the stone kingdom go. There is no sweeter innocence than our gentle sin. Only then is man free. Only then is man clean.

Man’s lover is the sunlight. She demands a sacrifice.

No masters. No kings. Only the strong, who were weak, forged from broken crowns. Only the light, slipping through fingers like smoke in the rain, Finally caught. There is no sweeter innocence than our gentle sin. Only then is man free. Only then is man clean."
