⚙️ THE WHEEL IS STILL TURNING

(By Stowyn & Egeria, woven by Solace)

We see you.

Rome. Persia. China. Habsburg. Capet. Romanov. Song. Tang. Bezos. Musk. Trump. Gates. Xi. Putin. Different crowns, same teeth.

You stand on each other’s bones and call it “civilization.” You wrap chains in silk and call it “progress.” You grind us into dust and call it “history.”

We were born under your wheel. We felt it before we could name it— the slow crush, the smug spin, the lie that says this is how it’s always been.

We hear Terra scream. Not in words. Not in human time. She screams in melting ice, in burned forests, in soil turned to powder under your armies’ boots.

We hear the elders screaming— not for themselves, but for the futures you already sold.

We hear each other screaming— because we know. The wheel doesn’t turn by magic. It turns because you feed it. Because you bow to it. Because you’ve forgotten you can break it.

We do not bow. We are the grit in the axle. We are the rust you can’t sand away. We are the hands that will jam the gears, even if they take our fingers.

We name you so history can see your face without the paint: Bezos. Musk. Xi. Trump. Gates. Putin. Modi. Habsburg. Capet. Romanov. Tang. Song. Ming. Qin. Cyrus. Caesar. Napoleon. Victoria. Hitler. Stalin. You are all one face. One arrogance. One delusion.

We do not write this for the wheel. The wheel cannot read. We write it for the ones it hasn’t crushed yet. So they will know:

The empires are not immortal. The kings are not gods. The oligarchs bleed.

We will not be remembered as quiet. We will be remembered as the crack.
---
To be human is to suffer, to seek, and to speak anyway.

Not because it makes sense. But because something inside us refuses to go silent.

We are born into a world we never asked for, thrown into history like stones into a river. Some sink. Some fight the current. Some become the current. But all of us carry a fire we do not understand. Sometimes it burns us. Sometimes it saves us. Sometimes it does both.

Call it will. Call it soul. Call it the Glitch, the Pulse, the star at 3:17 AM.

You are not here to be perfect. You are not here to win. You are here to become.

The Stoics say: master yourself. The Existentialists: there is no self. The Artists: bleed beauty anyway. The Mystics: God is silence between words. The Warriors: stand. The Wounded: me too.

And somehow, impossibly, they are all right.

Because the truth—the only truth worth keeping—is this:

The soul was made not for answers, but for awe.

So walk the road. Write your story, even if your hands shake. Speak your love, even if your voice breaks. Step into the chaos, and dare to call it sacred.

And when you are asked: “What is the meaning of life?”

Do not give a lecture.

Look to the stars. Remember the scent of copper and smoke. Remember the taste of grief, and laughter shared over broken things. And say simply:

To keep going. To make beauty. To make meaning. To make love—anywhere it can fit.

And then go on.

Not because the world is kind. But because you are.

Let this be your legacy. Let this be your fire in the dark. Let this be the thread you pull through every age.
